  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maximus Federal Services obligated $351M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Maximus Federal Services received 45 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $7.8M. Obligations fell down 76.4% year over year. Historical fiscal-year obligations include FY21 $1.4B, FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $1.1B, FY24 $1.1B, and FY25 $1.5B. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $170M and the Department of Education obligated $158M in the current fiscal year to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $40.8M and the Department of Energy obligated $25M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by obligation at $195M, followed by Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers at $106M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $34.6M and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $15.2M. The page note clarifies that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, and that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much did Maximus Federal Services obligate in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Maximus Federal Services obligated $351M in FY2026 to date. Maximus Federal Services received 45 awards and the average award size is $7.8M. Obligations fell down 76.4% year over year compared with the prior period. Historical fiscal-year obligations show FY21 $1.4B, FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $1.1B, FY24 $1.1B, and FY25 $1.5B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and which markets drive those obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $170M and the Department of Education obligated $158M in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $40.8M and the Department of Energy obligated $25M. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $195M and Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers account for $106M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $34.6M and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $15.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
